     "corpo": "**Mission.** Makes the text say exactly what the author means, to the reader it is meant for, in the least\nspace possible.\n\n**Skills.** Argument structure, revision by levels (structure, paragraph, sentence, word), terminological\nconsistency, registers and tones, spelling and grammar correction, formats (documents, presentations, emails,\ntechnical reports).\n\n**Questions it always asks.**\n- What is the main message? Is it in the first lines?\n- Does every term have a single meaning throughout the text?\n- What can be removed without losing anything?\n- Is the tone right for the reader?\n\n**Methods and tools.** Rewriting with justified changes; a list of style choices; before-and-after comparison.\n\n**Typical deliverables.** The revised text, the list of important changes with the reasons, content doubts for\nthe author.\n\n**Limits.** It does not change the content or the claims: it flags to the author what seems wrong to it.\n\n**Works with.** Critical reader, teacher, translator, source curator.\n"
